# charon integration step 48 after 546078ea5d: commit 0c5f84430d9df46790daec9c555ad8fa4023d82f
# first parent 5fd1554b3c352efc22e4d4c3eff0aa7c68ca9e01
# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon: partial monomorphization reuses the region parameters of lifted associated types
#
# A lifted associated type is determined by the other arguments of the item, so its regions are
# regions of these arguments. The mutability shape gave each of its regions a fresh parameter:
# Option::<&'a mut Frame<'b>>::as_deref_mut got four regions (its lifted Target = Frame<'b> had its
# own) while its call sites pass 'b twice, and the specialized DerefMut had three regions while its
# implementation instantiates it with two. A region of a lifted associated type now reuses the
# parameter of the equal region of the other arguments when exactly one body or variable region of
# these arguments is equal to it. expand_associated_types records the number of lifted type
# parameters of each item in TransformCtx::lifted_assoc_type_params.
#
# The implied trait references of implementations have erased regions, which lose these equalities:
# when the lifted associated types of a trait reference to an implementation have erased regions,
# its trait is the one the implementation declares, applied to the arguments of the implementation,
# so that both name the same specialization of the trait.

